1
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,197
What the hell?

2
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:27,500
Where am I?

3
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,400
I remember being at Egil's place.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:36,020
Then I left with Asuna.

5
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:40,320
But I can't remember what happened next.

6
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,580
My clothes.

7
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,560
Am I in a game right now?

8
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,400
Command!

9
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,300
Log out?

10
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:10,600
Way too realistic to be a 3d
object so this ain't a game.

11
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,717
Am I dreaming?

12
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,357
Wait, that's it.

13
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,717
This is the underworld.

14
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,957
I'm hooked up to the STL.

15
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:21,957
But that can't be right.

16
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:26,997
If I'm diving in the STL, my memories
of the real world should be blocked.

17
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:30,940
and I can still remember hanging
out with Asuna and Xenon.

18
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:34,440
Kikwoka! Higa!

19
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,440
Anyone, abort the dive!

20
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:40,460
I think there's something wrong in here!

21
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,720
This is too real for VR.

22
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:13,417
What was that I don't know why but

23
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,020
it felt so nostalgic and frustrating?

24
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,150
The end of the day?

25
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:35,577
I'm feeling like I'm tired!

26
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,037
A hundred and more dark!

27
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,757
Let's begin with my own!

28
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,097
I can't stop it!

29
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:44,597
I can't stop it!

30
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:47,337
I can't stop it! I'll be down!

31
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:48,637
I can't stop it!

32
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,337
My spirit is going to block the magma!

33
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,337
I can't stop it!

34
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:54,580
There's a lot of pain in the air!

35
00:02:57,080 --> 00:03:01,437
I hear a voice that I'm calling!

36
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,057
To you the figures!

37
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:06,057
I'm going to show you the beginning!

38
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,877
I'm going to see you in the beginning!

39
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:13,477
I'm going to see you in the beginning!

40
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,497
Shine your song, my diamond!

41
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:19,357
I'm going to cry,
darling! I'm going to cry?

42
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,180
Oh, my God.

43
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,920
Who are you?

44
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,980
Are you from around here?

45
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,700
Is he a tester like me?

46
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:43,340
Or is he an NPC?

47
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:48,420
Do you have a name?

48
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,660
Um, yeah, I got one.

49
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:55,820
It's Kirito.

50
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,090
Kirito?

51
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:02,597
I came from the forest over there, but
I'm not sure where I am or anything.

52
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,600
The forest?

53
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:05,427
Oh, you mean from the south?

54
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,815
Did you walk all the way from Zakaria?

55
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,620
No, I don't think so.

56
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:14,060
I mean, it's like, I
don't know how I got here.

57
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,360
I can't remember. What?

58
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,697
Then where do you live?

59
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,977
Can you remember the name of the town?

60
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,160
Um, no, everything's a blank.

61
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,800
I woke up and I was in the forest.

62
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:29,757
I heard the stories, but I never thought
I'd meet a real life lost child of Vecta.

63
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:30,958
I can't believe it.

64
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,630
Huh?

65
00:05:32,713 --> 00:05:33,543
What's a Vecta?

66
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,997
Wait, isn't that what they're
called where you're from?

67
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,380
When someone disappears from a village,

68
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:42,037
then suddenly turns up
in a forest or a field.

69
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,397
That's what they're called.

70
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,617
A child of Vecta.

71
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:48,960
The Dark God Vecta likes to prank
humans by snatching them up,

72
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:53,316
stealing their memories and plopping
them down somewhere far from home.

73
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:57,200
Oh, I guess that must have
been what happened to me then.

74
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,820
His responses are way
too natural for an NPC.

75
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:04,046
I'll try the direct approach.

76
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:08,060
Anyway, I'm kind of stuck, so...

77
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,080
I want to leave.

78
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:15,980
Yes, I'm sure you do.

79
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:21,964
I think I know how to help you.

80
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:24,917
The forest is huge and easy
to get lost in, though.

81
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,017
I can show you a path that leads north.

82
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,717
As long as you stick to it, you won't...

83
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,630
Sorry.

84
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,860
I want to log out now.

85
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:34,170
Log out?

86
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,816
What does that mean?

87
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,190
Damn it.

88
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,957
It's slang, you know?

89
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:45,500
It's like a faster way of saying I
need to find a place to stay. Really?

90
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,545
I never heard that one before.

91
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,200
Now what?

92
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:55,080
He could be a tester, but if he is,
his memories are definitely blocked.

93
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:58,597
My village is called Rulid
and it's beyond those trees,

94
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,437
but we don't get many travelers,

95
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,579
so there's no win.

96
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:05,997
I think if we go to the church and
explain your situation to Sister Azalea,

97
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,637
she might agree to put you up.

98
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,300
Oh, okay then.

99
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,073
I'll go to your village and talk to her.

100
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,290
Wait a moment.

101
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,177
You're a stranger in these parts.

102
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:21,436
I don't think the guards at the gate
are going to let you in so easily.

103
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:22,877
You know what?

104
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,697
If I go with you and talk to
them, they should understand.

105
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:27,117
That'd be great if you did.

106
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,030
Thanks a lot.

107
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,077
But I can't go yet.

108
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,984
I have to finish my work first.

109
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,560
And I won't be done
for another four hours.

110
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:38,760
I don't mind. I can wait.

111
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:41,960
That is, as long as it's
okay with you. Of course.

112
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:44,917
Have a seat anywhere you
like, and I'll get to work.

113
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,294
Oh, I haven't told you my name, have I?

114
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:48,690
No.

115
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:54,000
My name is Eugeo. How'd you do?

116
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,030
Eugeo?

117
00:07:56,113 --> 00:07:56,943
Sounds familiar.

118
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,800
What's wrong, Sir Kirito?

119
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,650
Nothing.

120
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:05,750
thing.

121
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:08,700
Oh, and you can just call me Kirito. Okay.

122
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:11,374
Nice to make your acquaintance, Kirito.

123
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,217
That's right.

124
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:20,637
You must be hungry.

125
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,497
Oh, thanks a lot.

126
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,617
He's definitely not an NPC.

127
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:25,880
Still not sure

128
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,157
if he's a test player, though.

129
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,720
Or maybe this isn't VR.

130
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,537
Maybe this is real.

131
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:36,297
The only good The good thing about
this bread is it keeps for a long time,

132
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,040
but just to be safe.

133
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,560
Okay, let me try that.

134
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:50,400
That settles it.

135
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:53,297
This ain't reality or
a parallel dimension.

136
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:54,380
It's VR.

137
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,680
Hey Kirito. What?

138
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:59,704
Did you forget how to use
the Stacia window too?

139
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,600
No, course not.

140
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,877
You can take your time
eating it if you want.

141
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,901
It still has plenty of life left.

142
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:14,744
If this were summer, you can bet
it wouldn't keep nearly as long.

143
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:17,810
Huh?

144
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:19,730
Holy!

145
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,380
It's not very good, huh?

146
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:26,537
I get them from the bakery
every morning on my way here,

147
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:29,037
but so early they only have day-old bread,

148
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:32,217
and I don't have time to go
back at noon for fresh ones.

149
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:33,130
That sucks.

150
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:37,149
Do you have time to make lunch
or have someone else make it?

151
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:43,301
Well, actually, someone used to bring me
my lunch every day, but that was years ago.

152
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,530
Oh, well.

153
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,500
So why'd they stop?

154
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,540
She was my childhood friend.

155
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,460
She was the same age as me.

156
00:09:56,980 --> 00:10:00,220
When we were little, we
played together all the time.

157
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:06,020
And after I received my calling, she would
bring me lunch every day without fail.

158
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:14,040
But then, because of me, the two of
us went to explore a cave up north.

159
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:18,017
And by accident, she crossed the
boundary into the Dark Territory.

160
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:20,860
A place no human is
allowed to enter, ever.

161
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:23,340
The Taboo Index forbids it.

162
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:24,960
Taboo Index?

163
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:29,680
The next day, an Integrity
Knight came to our village.

164
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:34,640
and he took her to Senator to be executed.

165
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:39,840
But I still believe she's alive, Kirito.

166
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,460
I know it.

167
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:45,840
Somewhere in Senator, Alice is alive.

168
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:47,570
Alice.

169
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:49,560
I know that name.

170
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:52,830
Alice.

171
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:55,440
I'm sorry.

172
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,497
I didn't mean to dump all that on you.

173
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:02,345
I know we just met and all, but
it feels like we're old friends.

174
00:11:03,180 --> 00:11:04,010
That's okay.

175
00:11:04,093 --> 00:11:04,923
I don't mind.

176
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,120
So, why don't you go find her?

177
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,908
Go to Senator or wherever.

178
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:11,218
See if she's there.

179
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,680
Even if I had the fastest
horse in the land,

180
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,297
it would take a week
to get there from here.

181
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:20,380
Then throw some clothes
and food in a bag and walk.

182
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,320
If I could do that, I would.

183
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:25,540
But I can't just abandon my calling.

184
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:27,660
The Taboo Index forbids it.

185
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:29,010
You know that.

186
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,600
Oh, right. You got a point.

187
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:33,910
Um...

188
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:38,680
Sorry to be nosy, but about how
long ago did all this happen anyway?

189
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,040
It was my 11th summer six years ago.

190
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,081
Want some water?

191
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:48,940
Thanks. Maybe later.

192
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,757
Well, lunch is over, so I
better get back to work.

193
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,837
I still have to meet my quota for today.

194
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,332
I'll just kick back till you finish then.

195
00:11:57,660 --> 00:12:00,840
By the way, your calling,
what is it? You'll see.

196
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:02,520
It's not very exciting.

197
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:28,400
So like your callings to chop down trees?

198
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:32,437
Yeah, officially my title's
supposed to be woodcutter.

199
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:33,440
The problem is,

200
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:37,497
I haven't cut a single tree down in the
seven years since I received my calling.

201
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:38,410
What?

202
00:12:38,493 --> 00:12:40,085
My job's to work on this tree.

203
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,927
It's called the Gigas Cedar.

204
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:44,767
The villagers call it
something else, though.

205
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,140
The Demon Tree.

206
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:49,357
They call it that because
it sucks up all of

207
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:52,087
Terraria's blessings
from the land around it.

208
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,957
Rulid has always wanted to
plant more wheat fields,

209
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,737
but as long as this is here,
nothing good will grow.

210
00:12:57,820 --> 00:13:01,017
The village had that dragon bone
axe sent from the capital and

211
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:04,957
appointed a woodcutter to work on it
every day till the tree came down.

212
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,100
That's my job.

213
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:10,680
So, for the past seven years now,
you've been chopping away at it?

214
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:15,520
After all that time, that's
as far as you got? Hardly.

215
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:19,267
I'm actually a
seventh-generation woodcutter.

216
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:20,878
That's our calling.

217
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:23,857
Someone's been chopping
away on it every single day.

218
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,500
For 300 years, in fact.

219
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,500
For 300 years?

220
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,377
Hey, Yu-Gi-Oh.

221
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:37,060
Mind if I take a crack at it? Huh?

222
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:41,099
I mean, you did give me
half your lunch, didn't you?

223
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:44,177
So it's only fair I should
pick up half your work.

224
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,540
Oh, I don't know.

225
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,917
I mean, the taboo index doesn't
say I can't have someone help,

226
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,176
even though it is my calling and all.

227
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,129
Try it, but it's much
harder than it looks.

228
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,657
I won't know till I try.

229
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:57,799
Here goes nothing.

230
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,560
You don't have to laugh that hard.

231
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,080
I'm sorry about that.

232
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:27,232
You put way too much tension
into your shoulders and hips.

233
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:30,305
Relax and let the momentum
do the work for you.

234
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,720
That's right.

235
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,720
This is a virtual world.

236
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:39,160
It's not about my real
ability, but my avatars.

237
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,140
Sword skill? Smash!

238
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:02,220
Whoa, that was a nice hit.

239
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:06,100
Go on, give it another
shot before you forget.

240
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,270
Fifty!

241
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,420
Okay, that's 1,000 strikes.

242
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:14,970
Really?

243
00:15:15,053 --> 00:15:16,740
We did that many today?

244
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:18,270
Uh-huh.

245
00:15:18,353 --> 00:15:22,320
500 for me and 500 for you at
the thousand I did this morning,

246
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,284
and that's 2,000 strikes total.

247
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,695
That's the daily quota for my calling.

248
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,640
Oh, my God.

249
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,221
You're a natural at this, Kirito.

250
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:34,046
Thanks to your skill, I
had an easy day today.

251
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,057
I don't know about that.

252
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:40,611
I bet you would have had it cut down
by now if I wasn't here messing around.

253
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:43,090
Think so?

254
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:45,104
Then you need to see something.

255
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:50,880
It's only gone down by
about 50 since last month.

256
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:52,632
That's normal, actually.

257
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:54,260
It's a strong tree.

258
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:57,077
So what if we didn't make
a lot of progress today?

259
00:15:57,160 --> 00:16:00,866
In the end, it doesn't really
make much of a difference at all.

260
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,530
Let's go.

261
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,720
Wait, you forgot to lock it. What for?

262
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:09,260
What do you mean?

263
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:10,933
Someone could steal it.

264
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,297
Now who'd do that?

265
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:16,556
It clearly states in the Taboo Index
that theft is forbidden, remember?

266
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:18,093
Oh, yeah, that's right.

267
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:20,517
Come on, I'll show you my village.

268
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,820
Um, but...

269
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,500
Hey, wait up!

270
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,560
Hey, U-J-O.

271
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:46,754
Who's your new friend?

272
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,497
Hey, Zink.

273
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:50,857
This is Kirito.

274
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:53,560
I think he's a lost child of Vecta.

275
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,480
That true?

276
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,327
You can't remember anything?

277
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,760
Um, no.

278
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,117
Did you forget your calling, too?

279
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,140
Yeah, I guess.

280
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,780
It was probably a lousy calling anyway.

281
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,260
Bet it was as lame as Eugeo's here.

282
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:13,069
He's got one of the most pointless
callings in all the land.

283
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:17,437
now mine i'm a man at arms and swordsman

284
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:21,437
that's my calling man i'm a swordsman

285
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:27,660
a swordsman a scrawny weak-looking pipsqueak
like you you can't even lift a sword

286
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,940
go on then show us your skill

287
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,980
Let's see how I do with this.

288
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:02,580
No way.

289
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,180
That was a light effect.

290
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,780
There's sword skills here.

291
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,880
That was amazing.

292
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,974
I didn't know you had skills like that.

293
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:18,000
Maybe you were a sentinel
in some big city.

294
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,840
I don't know. Maybe.

295
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:23,400
Zink, will you let Kirito in?

296
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,188
I'd like to show him
around the village now.

297
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:36,660
I'm tired.

298
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:39,400
Well, we're here. Finally.

299
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:41,920
Is this really okay?

300
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:46,377
I mean, everyone's just going to accept
I'm one of those lost Vecta kids?

301
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,872
Isn't that what you are?

302
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,320
Yeah, I guess so.

303
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:54,064
Let's talk to the sister
and get you sorted out.

304
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,120
What do you boys want?

305
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:08,420
Uh, I...

306
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:17,389
Here, I brought you a
pillow and a blanket.

307
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,485
Prayers begin at 6 o
'clock, breakfast is at 7.

308
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:24,493
I'll come check on you, but
please try to get up on time.

309
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:26,288
Do not be late for prayers.

310
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:29,329
You do not want to make
Sister Azealia mad.

311
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:32,856
Also, we have a curfew after
life's out, so mind that.

312
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:34,280
She saw us! Run!

313
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,630
Honestly.

314
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:39,038
Now then, do you have any questions?

315
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:40,160
No, I'm good.

316
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:42,091
Thanks for setting me up.

317
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,054
Well, good night then.

318
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:48,260
You know how to put out
the lamp, right? Yeah.

319
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,460
Good night, Selka.

320
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:04,920
This ain't the real world.

321
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:09,200
And as far as I can tell, none
of the villagers are NPCs.

322
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,801
But they can't be testers either.

323
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:15,037
There'd have to be dozens of
STLs for them to log in with,

324
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:17,120
and I know there aren't that many.

325
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,360
What did Yu-Gi-Oh say?

326
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:26,465
According to him, more than 300
years have passed in this world.

327
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:31,660
He spent the last six as a woodcutter
here, and remembers his childhood here too.

328
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:36,080
If that's true, then him and the others...

329
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,030
Hmm?

330
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:44,090
Oh.

331
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:52,677
Yu-Gi-Oh and the villagers were
raised here from the start.

332
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:57,640
But the only way that could happen is
if Wrath copied the souls of babies.

333
00:20:58,940 --> 00:20:59,770
Babies.

334
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,373
Artificial Fluctlights.

335
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,817
It's hard to believe, but
there's no other explanation.

336
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,940
But why would Wrath do that?

337
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:12,846
And how fast would they have to accelerate
time to get this world to this point?

338
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:19,300
And what if I'm stuck here
forever and never get back home?

339
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:25,660
Maybe I can get in touch with Kikuoka
if I can get to a bigger city!

340
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:29,117
I need money to travel
and right now I got none

341
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:31,900
and I don't know enough
about this world yet.

342
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:40,720
If I had some help I could get to
Senator and find some answers there.

343
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:24,980
Let's go.

344
00:23:26,660 --> 00:23:29,200
Me Alice to you

345
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:38,060
Next time, The End Mountains
